<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kalashoka</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">4th century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a> · Also known as Kakavarna</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kalashoka was a king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magadha">Magadha</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shishunaga-dynasty">Shishunaga dynasty</a> in the 4th century BCE, called Kakavarna in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/puranas">Puranas</a>. Buddhist tradition says the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-buddhist-council">Second Buddhist Council</a> was held at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vaishali">Vaishali</a> under his patronage, about a century after the death of the Buddha. He is said to have moved the capital back to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pataliputra">Pataliputra</a> and was reportedly murdered, after which the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nanda-dynasty">Nanda dynasty</a> came to power.</p></div>
